    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "One can now apply Little’s law, E[LFCFS] = λE[K]E[WFCFS] to find a first expression for the mean number of waiting customers in the system. It remains to find the average travel time E[T] to a waiting customer. The travel time under the FCFS service policy is hard to analyse, as this depends on the state of the system at the arrival instant, as well as future arrivals. Instead, we remark that the average travel time to a tagged customer is the same for the FCFS model and polling model. This is due to the fact that the sum of the travel times to all customers is the same. We can therefore focus on the original system to derive E[T]. Recall (1), stating that the server is within a small interval [x,x + dx] with probability [ρπ(x) + 1 − ρ]dx . Therefore, we have:"
